  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Defense obligated $309B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense recorded 2,547,101 contract awards with an average award size of $121K. Obligations fell 37.2% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show a decline from prior peaks: FY25 totaled $492B, FY24 totaled $446B, and FY23 totaled $457B, while FY22 totaled $414B and FY21 totaled $387B. The largest spending categories in FY2026 to date include Aircraft Manufacturing at $38.5B, Engineering Services at $26.9B, and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $26.9B. Ship Building and Repairing received $18.9B and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences received $21.9B. The top vendors for FY2026 to date include LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $12.5B, LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $10.8B, and ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $10.8B. The Department of Defense continues to fund a mix of manufacturing, services, construction, and health-related contracts in the current fiscal-year-to-date period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date contracting compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $309B in FY2026 to date, compared with $492B in FY25 and $446B in FY24. The Department of Defense recorded obligations of $457B in FY23, $414B in FY22, and $387B in FY21. Obligations fell 37.2% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors account for the largest FY2026 to date obligations?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest industry with $38.5B in obligations, followed by Engineering Services at $26.9B and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $26.9B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $21.9B and Ship Building and Repairing accounted for $18.9B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION is the top vendor at $12.5B, followed by LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $10.8B and ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $10.8B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Defense spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense obligated $309B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense recorded 2,547,101 contract awards and an average award size of $121K. Obligations fell 37.2% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Defense buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense buys a mix of manufacturing, services, construction, and health-related goods and services. Aircraft Manufacturing received $38.5B, Engineering Services received $26.9B, Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing received $26.9B, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences received $21.9B, and Ship Building and Repairing received $18.9B. Other top categories include Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $13B and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $12.8B."
